      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Last time we ended with two beakers that look exactly the same. One holds pure water, and one holds salt water. Now switch the hotplates on. The pure water heats up, starts to boil at a hundred degrees, and then stays at a hundred for as long as it boils. The salt water starts boiling a little higher, at about a hundred and one, and as it boils, its temperature keeps creeping up. Same look, different behaviour. So what can a melting or boiling observation tell us about a sample, and what can't it tell us?",
      "humanListening": "pending"
