      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's how that shows up in data. Sample A melts sharply at three hundred and twenty seven degrees. All of it turns to liquid at that one temperature. Sample B starts to soften at sixty degrees, and it isn't fully liquid until eighty, a twenty degree range. A sharp melting point is consistent with a pure substance. A melting range is physical evidence that a sample is probably a mixture. Candle wax behaves like sample B, because wax is a mixture of many similar compounds.",
