        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "But be careful with the sharp one. Consistent with pure isn't the same as proof of pure. A few mixtures boil at one steady temperature, just like a pure substance, and you'll meet one when we distil ethanol. Boiling points also change with air pressure. High on a mountain, pure water boils below a hundred degrees. And one melting point can match more than one substance. So chemists state the pressure, and they check at least two independent properties before they conclude anything.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
