      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's how that works. A white solid melts sharply at eight hundred and one degrees. Its density is two point one six grams per cubic centimetre, and it dissolves in water. Now check a data table. Sodium chloride melts at eight hundred and one degrees and has a density of two point one six. Two independent properties match, and it dissolves, so it's very likely sodium chloride. That's not certain, but it's much stronger evidence than one number.",
