      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "That last point matters. Melting, boiling and sublimation are physical changes. The particles spread out or pack together, but they stay the same particles, so cooling can reverse the change. A chemical change makes a new substance. Burn a strip of magnesium, and the shiny metal becomes a white powder, magnesium oxide, with completely different properties. So a change of state alone is never evidence of a chemical reaction. You need evidence of a new substance.",
