      "pronunciationText": "Boiling point is a physical property. A physical property is something you can measure or observe without turning the substance into a different substance. Melting point is the temperature where a solid turns into a liquid. Boiling point is the temperature where a liquid boils, forming gas all the way through it, not just at the surface. Density, solubility and electrical conductivity are physical properties too. A pure substance has its own fixed values, which is why chemists can look them up in a data table.",
